ANSWER: {"answer": "Found a suitable beginner's computer science course covering Python on Coursera: 'Python 3 Programming Specialization' by the University of Michigan (https://www.coursera.org/specializations/python-3-programming). It is listed under Computer Science > Software Development, rated Beginner level ('No prior experience required'), has a 4.8-star rating from 23,081 reviews, 285,422 learners enrolled, and is a 5-course series taking about 3 months (10 hrs/week). It teaches Python 3 basics through advanced concepts (lists, functions, debugging, fetching data from APIs, etc.). I located it via Coursera's search (query: 'beginner computer science python', filtered by Level = Beginner) directly from the homepage search bar, without signing in, creating an account, or entering any personal/payment data — stopped right at the course info page before any enrollment step that would require login."}
